# Who must approve a pull request, by path. The LAST matching line wins.
# Everyone listed must have Write access to the repository, or the line is ignored.
# Replace the handles below. These lines are the Kant Lab's arrangement; change them to yours.

# Default: the instructor, or any one of the default reviewers beside them, approves
# everything not matched below.
*                    @INSTRUCTOR @REVIEWER-1 @REVIEWER-2
# Who approves what is the instructor's decision alone, so this file needs the instructor.
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @INSTRUCTOR
# Personal sandboxes: no owner, so the author merges their own pull request.
/Individuals/
# The portal is the whole seminar's and has no owner: whoever makes a change merges it.
/portal/
# The shared data and how it is made have student owners, who approve each other's changes.
# Always include the instructor, so that a stuck change can be unblocked.
/portal/data/        @INSTRUCTOR @DATA-OWNER-1 @DATA-OWNER-2
/tools/              @INSTRUCTOR @DATA-OWNER-1 @DATA-OWNER-2
/sources/            @INSTRUCTOR @DATA-OWNER-1 @DATA-OWNER-2
